Reg 111(7): THE FOLLOWING NOTICES IN HINDI AND LOCAL LANGUAGE OF THE DISTRICT, SO DESIGNED AND PROTECTED AS TO BE EASILY LEGIBLE AT ALL TIMES, SHALL BE EXHIBITED AT THE FOLLOWING PLACES, namely —
(i) WHERE ELECTRICAL APPARATUS IS IN USE, A NOTICE FORBIDDING UNDESIGNATED PERSONS TO OPERATE OR OTHERWISE INTERFERE WITH SUCH APPARATUS;
(ii) IN THE INTERIOR OR AT THE SURFACE OF THE MINE WHERE A TELEPHONE OR OTHER MEANS OF COMMUNICATION IS PROVIDED, A NOTICE GIVING FULL INSTRUCTIONS TO THE PERSON AT THE SURFACE OF THE MINE DESIGNATED TO EFFECT THE DISCONNECTION OF THE SUPPLY OF ELECTRICITY TO THE MINE.

Reg 106: SWITCHGEAR AND ALL TERMINALS, CABLE ENDS, CABLE JOINTS AND CONNECTIONS TO APPARATUS SHALL BE TOTALLY ENCLOSED and shall be constructed, installed and maintained so as to comply with —
(i) all parts shall be of MECHANICAL STRENGTH SUFFICIENT TO RESIST ROUGH USAGE;
(ii) all conductors and contact areas shall be of ADEQUATE CURRENT-CARRYING CAPACITY and all joints PROPERLY SOLDERED or otherwise efficiently made;
(iii) THE LODGEMENT OF ANY MATTER LIKELY TO DIMINISH THE INSULATION OR AFFECT THE WORKING OF ANY SWITCHGEAR SHALL BE PREVENTED;
(iv) ALL LIVE PARTS SHALL BE SO PROTECTED OR ENCLOSED as to prevent persons accidentally coming into contact with them and to PREVENT DANGER FROM ARCS, SHORT-CIRCUITS, FIRE, WATER, GAS OR OIL;
(v) WHERE THERE MAY BE RISK OF IGNITING GAS, COAL-DUST, OIL OR OTHER INFLAMMABLE MATERIAL, ALL PARTS SHALL BE SO PROTECTED AS TO PREVENT OPEN SPARKING; and
(vi) EVERY SWITCH OR CIRCUIT-BREAKER SHALL BE SO CONSTRUCTED AS TO BE CAPABLE OF OPENING THE CIRCUIT IT CONTROLS AND DEALING WITH ANY SHORT-CIRCUIT WITHOUT DANGER.

Reg 108: All cables, other than flexible cables for portable or transportable apparatus, shall fulfil —
(i) covered with INSULATING MATERIAL and EFFICIENTLY PROTECTED FROM MECHANICAL DAMAGE and SUPPORTED AT SUFFICIENTLY FREQUENT INTERVALS;
(ii)(a) no cables other than concentric, single core, two core or multi core cables PROTECTED BY A METALLIC COVERING and containing ALL THE CONDUCTORS OF A CIRCUIT shall be used WHERE THE VOLTAGE EXCEEDS 125 V or where an Inspector considers there is risk of igniting gas or COAL DUST;
(iv) THE METALLIC COVERING OF EVERY CABLE SHALL BE — (a) ELECTRICALLY AND MECHANICALLY CONTINUOUS THROUGHOUT; (b) EARTHED by connection to the earthing system; (c) EFFICIENTLY PROTECTED AGAINST CORROSION where necessary; (d) OF A CONDUCTIVITY at all parts and joints AT LEAST EQUAL TO FIFTY PER CENT of the conductivity of the largest conductor enclosed; (e) where there may be risk of igniting gas or coal-dust, SO CONSTRUCTED AS TO PREVENT OPEN SPARKING;
(v) cables connected to motors, transformers, switchgear shall be installed so that they are MECHANICALLY PROTECTED by securely attaching the metallic covering to the apparatus, and THE INSULATING MATERIAL AT EACH CABLE END IS EFFICIENTLY SEALED;
(vi) PROPERLY CONSTRUCTED GLANDS OR BUSHES shall be provided where necessary to prevent abrasion or secure gas-tightness.
